---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
const mc = 'https://mentorcruise.com/mentor/armaganamcalar/'
---

<Base title="Mentoring" description="One-to-one mentoring with Armağan Amcalar for engineers, engineering managers and founders, through MentorCruise.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>Mentoring</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I've been mentoring engineers, engineering managers and founders since 2012. Today I do it one-to-one through MentorCruise, alongside my work as a
        fractional CTO.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href={mc}>Book on MentorCruise</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/?topic=mentoring">Ask a question first</a>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>What I can help with</h2></div>
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h3>Building or scaling a startup</h3>
          <p>Technical, operational and strategic decisions when you're the one who has to make them, often for the first time.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Leading engineers</h3>
          <p>Building an engineering culture, hiring, growing people, and lining technical goals up with what the business needs.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Architecture</h3>
          <p>Hard design decisions, from IoT and embedded systems to product roadmaps and multi-cloud architecture.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Your own career</h3>
          <p>Getting from mid-level to senior, from senior to lead, or deciding whether management is for you.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Levelling up a team</h3>
          <p>Masterclass training and practical guidance on code quality, review and collaboration.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Hiring for a critical role</h3>
          <p>A second opinion from someone who has interviewed and hired engineers for fifteen years.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>How it works</h2></div>
      <dl class="facts">
        <dt>Ongoing</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>Two 60-minute calls a month, plus chat</strong>
          <span>Unlimited questions between calls, answered within two days. Month to month, with a free seven-day trial and no contract.</span>
        </dd>
        <dt>One-off</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>A single 60-minute “ask me anything” call</strong>
          <span>For one decision, one review or one conversation you need to have with someone outside your company.</span>
        </dd>
        <dt>Practical</dt>
        <dd>
          <strong>In English or Turkish, on Berlin time</strong>
          <span>Usually available Monday to Friday, 09:00 to 17:00 CET. Booking, pricing and payment are handled by MentorCruise.</span>
        </dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="narrow prose" style="margin-inline:0">
        <blockquote class="pull">
          “Armagan is a Motivation Generator. He pushes you to think and ask critical questions to yourself.”
        </blockquote>
        <p class="meta">Akin, after an Ask Me Anything session · MentorCruise, October 2025</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><h2>If you need more than a mentor</h2></div>
      <div class="cols">
        <div>
          <h3>Fractional CTO</h3>
          <p>
            When the company needs someone accountable for technology part-time, I take that role through <a href="/coyotiv/">Coyotiv</a>, with a team behind me
            when there is work to be built.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Learning to code from the start</h3>
          <p>
            The <a href="https://coyotiv.com/school/">Coyotiv School of Software Engineering</a> is a 14-week live program I designed and teach, for people
            entering the profession.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Lonca</h3>
          <p>A voluntary, non-profit software craftsmanship school I started in 2014, which trains women engineers through apprenticeship.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
